<title>GREECE: Triaina, Aspis lead Greek money market funds in Q1.</title>
<headline>Triaina, Aspis lead Greek money market funds in Q1.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Triaina and Aspis Pronia were leading Greece's 31-strong money market funds in the first quarter of 1997 with year-to-date returns of 4.79 percent and 3.38 percent respectively, the association of institutional investors said.</p>
<p>Money market funds under management reached 2.819 trillion drachmas at end-March, up 25.31 percent year-to-date and 5.60 percent month-on-month, it said.</p>
<p>Money market funds had the biggest market share in terms of total assets in the mutual fund industry with 58.91 percent, it said.</p>
<p>Greece's capital market commission has asked all mutual funds to comply with new regulations pertaining to their fund classification by September.</p>
<p>Money market funds have to invest at least 65 percent of their assets in money market instruments.</p>
